  "slug": "john-lennon-travels-to-carboneras-spain",
  "title": "18 September 1966: John Lennon travels to Carboneras, Spain",
  "date": "1966-09-18",
  "content": "<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\"><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><p>Following the <a href=\"/1966/09/05/john-lennon-flies-to-hanover-germany/\">initial filming period in Celle, West Germany</a>, <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a> travelled to southern Spain on this day to continue work on Richard Lester’s <em>How I Won The War</em>. <span id=\"more-6014\"></span></p><blockquote><div>I was always waiting for a reason to get out of The Beatles from the day I made <em>How I Won the War</em> in 1966. I just didn’t have the guts to do it, you see. Because I didn’t know where to go. I remember why I made the movie. I did it because The Beatles had stopped touring and I didn’t know what to do. Instead of going home and being with the family, I immediately went to Spain with Dick Lester because I couldn’t deal with not being continually onstage. That was the first time I thought, ‘My God, what do you do if this isn’t going on? What is there? There’s no life without it.’ And that’s when the seed was planted that I had to somehow get out of this, without being thrown out by the others. But I could never step out of the palace because it was too frightening.<p></p><p>I was really too scared to walk away. I was thinking, ‘Well, this is the end, really. There’s no more touring. That means there’s going to be a blank space in the future.’ At some time or other that’s when I started considering life without The Beatles – what would it be? And I spent that six weeks thinking about that: ‘What am I going to do? Am I going to be doing Vegas? But cabaret?’ I mean, where do you go? So that’s when I started thinking about it. But I could not think what it would be, or how I could do it. I didn’t even consider forming my own group or anything, because it didn’t enter my mind. Just what would I do when it stopped?</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">John Lennon<br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div><p>Lennon had the part of Private Gripweed in the film, which was released in 1967. He remained in Spain for seven weeks, initially staying at a small seafront apartment but later moving to a villa, Santa Isabel, near Almería.</p><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/1966/09/18/john-lennon-travels-to-carboneras-spain/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-1\" class=\"gallery galleryid-6014 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_07/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNjgiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTY4IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"168\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_07-168x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon on the set of How I Won The War, 1966\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_07-168x200.jpg 168w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_07-488x580.jpg 488w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_07.jpg 590w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 168px) 100vw, 168px\" data-attachment-id=\"23821\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_07/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_07.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"590,701\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon on the set of How I Won The War, 1966\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_0