n the set of How I Won The War, 1966\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04-580x580.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04-960x958.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04-768x766.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"23807\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,998\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon on the set of How I Won The War, 1966\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-how-i-won-the-war_04-960x958.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>Santa Isabel was owned by producer Sam Spiegal. Lennon stayed there with his wife <a href=\"/people/cynthia-lennon/\">Cynthia</a>, and The Beatles’ assistant <a href=\"/people/neil-aspinall/\">Neil Aspinall</a>. Also staying in the house was actor Michael Crawford, the star of <em>How I Won The War</em>, and his family.</p><p>Lennon also took his Rolls-Royce with blacked out windows to Spain. The car had a microphone and mounted loudspeaker, and Lennon took delight in surprising passers-by.</p><blockquote><div>When John went to make <em>How I Won The War</em> in Spain, he took the same car, which he virtually lived in. It had blacked-out windows and you could never see who was in it, so it was perfect. John didn’t come out of it – he just used to talk to the people outside through the microphone: ‘Get away from the car! Get away!’</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\"><a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/anthologypb\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Anthology</em></a></div>\n<!--[googlesitekit-end-of-content]--><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Page last updated:</strong> 3 March 2023</div></div></div><div class=\"on-this-day-wrapper\"><h3>Also on this day...</h3><ul><li>2024: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2024/09/18/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-chevalier-theatre-medford/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Chevalier Theatre, Medford</a></li><li>2018: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2018/09/18/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-floyd-l-maines-veterans-memorial-arena-binghamton/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Floyd L Maines Veterans Memorial Arena, Binghamton</a></li><li>2002: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2002/09/18/paul-mccartney-live-adopt-a-minefield-gala-los-angeles-2/\">Paul McCartney live: Adopt-A-Minefield Gala, Los Angeles</a></li><li>1993: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1993/09/18/paul-mccartney-live-westfalenhalle-dortmund-3/\">Paul McCartney live: Westfalenhalle, Dortmund</a></li><li>1991: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1991/09/18/recording-everybody-wins-angel-in-disguise-ringo-starr/\">Recording: Everybody Wins, Angel In Disguise by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1980: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1980/09/18/recording-every-man-has-a-woman-who-loves-him-just-like-starting-over-give-me-something-john-lennon-yoko-ono/\">Recording: Every Man Has A Woman Who Loves Him, (Just Like) Starting Over, Give Me Something by John Lennon and Yoko Ono</a></li><li>1980: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1980/09/18/photography-john-lennon-yoko-ono-kishin-shinoyama/\">Photography: John Lennon and Yoko Ono by Kishin Shinoyama</a></li><li>1975: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1975/09/18/wings-live-hammersmith-odeon-london-5/\">Wings live: Hammersmith Odeon, London</a></li><li>1974: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1974/09/18/recording-its-all-down-to-goodnight-vienna-no-no-song-ringo-starr/\">Recording: (It’s All Down To) Goodnight Vienna, No No Song by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/09/18/paul-mccartney-collapses-lagos/\">Paul McCartney collapses in Lagos</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/09/18/editing-compiling-mind-games-john-lennon-2/\">Editing, compiling: Mind Games by John Lennon</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/09/18/ringo-starr-buys-tittenhurst-park-from-john-lennon-yoko-ono/\">Ringo Starr buys Tittenhurst Park from John Lennon and Yoko Ono</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/09/18/recording-hi-hi-hi-wings-3/\">Recording: Hi, Hi, Hi by Wings</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/09/18/listening-party-abbey-road/\">Listening party: Abbey Road</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/09/18/paul-mccartney-performs-on-badfinger-rock-of-all-ages/\">Paul McCartney performs on Badfinger’s Rock Of All Ages</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/09/18/recording-mixing-birthday/\">Recording, mixing: Birthday</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/09/18/george-harrison-interview-new-musical-express-bbc/\">George Harrison is interviewed for New Musical Express and BBC</a></li><li>1967: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1967/09/18/filming-magical-mystery-tour-6/\">Filming: Magical Mystery Tour</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/09/18/live-memorial-auditorium-dallas/\">The Beatles live: Memorial Auditorium, Dallas</a></li><li>1960: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1960/09/18/live-indra-club-hamburg-33/\">The Beatles live: Indra Club, Hamburg</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div>",
  "textContent": "Following the initial filming period in Celle, West Germany, John Lennon travelled to southern Spain on this day to continue work on Richard Lester’s How I Won The War. I was always waiting for a reason to get out of The Beatles from the day I made How I Won the War in 1966. I just didn’t have the guts to do it, you see. Because I didn’t know where to go. I remember why I made the movie. I did it because The Beatles had stopped touring and I didn’t know what to do. Instead of going home and being with the family, I immediately went to Spain with Dick Lester because I couldn’t deal with not being continually onstage. That was the first time I thought, ‘My God, what do you do if this isn’t going on? What is there? There’s no life without it.’ And that’s when the seed was planted that I had to somehow get out of this, without being thrown out by the others. But I could never step out of the palace because it was too frightening.I was really too scared to walk away. I was thinking, ‘Well, this is the end, really. There’s no more touring. That means there’s going to be a blank space in the future.’ At some time or other that’s when I started considering life without The Beatles – what would it be? And I spent that six weeks thinking about that: ‘What am I going to do? Am I going to be doing Vegas? But cabaret?’ I mean, where do you go? So that’s when I started thinking about it. But I could not think what it would be, or how I could do it. I didn’t even consider forming my own group or anything, because it didn’t enter my mind. Just what would I do when it stopped?John Lennon\nAnthologyLennon had the part of Private Gripweed in the film, which was released in 1967. He remained in Spain for seven weeks, initially staying at a small seafront apartment but later moving to a villa, Santa Isabel, near Almería.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSanta Isabel was owned by producer Sam Spiegal. Lennon stayed there with his wife Cynthia, and The Beatles’ assistant Neil Aspinall. Also staying in the house was actor Michael Crawford, the star of How I Won The War, and his family.Lennon also took his Rolls-Royce with blacked out windows to Spain. The car had a microphone and mounted loudspeaker, and Lennon took delight in surprising passers-by.When John went to make How I Won The War in Spain, he took the same car, which he virtually lived in. It had blacked-out windows and you could never see who was in it, so it was perfect. John didn’t come out of it – he just used to talk to the people outside through the microphone: ‘Get away from the car! Get away!’Paul McCartney\nAnthology\nPage last updated: 3 March 2023Also on this day...2024: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Chevalier Theatre, Medford2018: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Floyd L Maines Veterans Memorial Arena, Binghamton2002: Paul McCartney live: Adopt-A-Minefield Gala, Los Angeles1993: Paul McCartney live: Westfalenhalle, Dortmund1991: Recording: Everybody Wins, Angel In Disguise by Ringo Starr1980: Recording: Every Man Has A Woman Who Loves Him, (Just Like) Starting Over, Give Me Something by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1980: Photography: John Lennon and Yoko Ono by Kishin Shinoyama1975: Wings live: Hammersmith Odeon, London1974: Recording: (It’s All Down To) Goodnight Vienna, No No Song by Ringo Starr1973: Paul McCartney collapses in Lagos1973: Editing, compiling: Mind Games by John Lennon1973: Ringo Starr buys Tittenhurst Park from John Lennon and Yoko Ono1972: Recording: Hi, Hi, Hi by Wings1969: Listening party: Abbey Road1969: Paul McCartney performs on Badfinger’s Rock Of All Ages1968: Recording, mixing: Birthday1968: George Harrison is interviewed for New Musical Express and BBC1967: Filming: Magical Mystery Tour1964: The Beatles live: Memorial Auditorium, Dallas1960: The Beatles live: Indra Club, HamburgWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
